      "tier": "high",
      "researcher_notes": "The state Title V permit 24-TV-005 and Polk County permits cover the Willow Creek data center at 550 SE White Crane Road in West Des Moines. A Polk County permit lists the contact as Microsoft. The older engines, emission units 1 to 66, are 66 Cummins diesel engines: one of 800 kilowatts, four of 2,000, sixty of 2,500 and one of 1,000. That is 159.8 MW. Emission units 67 to 86 are 20 Cummins QSK95-G9 engines of 3,000 kilowatts, 60 MW, permitted in 2024. This site is separate from Ginger East, which is at 1475 SE Maffitt Lake Road. The permit's own record keeping section separates Willow Creek (units 1 to 86) from Ginger East (units 101 to 201). Not found: start dates, and proof from imagery that the 20 newer engines are built. The point is the geocoded permit address, so the location is approximate. GEM has no Willow Creek record.",
